{"title":"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity_(Pure_magic!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity (Pure magic!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution:_Math_Bear_presents..._A_Fun_Algebra_Equation_Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution: Math Bear presents... A Fun Algebra Equation Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the largest real solution to the equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/1/db1b73306fa68b19b2005e9e87c15987a49ce36c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{x-3}+\\frac{5}{x-5}+\\frac{17}{x-17}+\\frac{19}{x-19}=x^2-11x-4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"391\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>There are positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d934cec9815769d8e29a8ed30ee2793a60093ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=a+\\sqrt{b+\\sqrt{c}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"143\" height=\"32\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first step is to notice that the 4 on the right hand side can simplify the terms on the left hand side. If we distribute 1 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d8110cb33b66cf04e287c5223a9f28434c706ed7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{x-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />, then the fraction becomes of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/6/176a3c6b866409b9770d870f902389d5c40d7ca8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x - 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"33\" />. A similar cancellation happens with the other four terms. If we assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is not the highest solution (which is true given the answer format) we can cancel the common factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> from both sides of the equation.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/b/5bb2f4ddca835e4cee220c1d9ff52306b062d1ea.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{x - 3} + \\frac{1}{x - 5} + \\frac{1}{x - 17} + \\frac{1}{x - 19} = x - 11\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Then, if we make the substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a148043b5022396af6d738a5d9e951463065a1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = x - 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" />, we can further simplify.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/0/c80e22d46d9a93160593f83e8f2a3ca6ee0a7fd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{y + 8} + \\frac{1}{y + 6} + \\frac{1}{y - 6} + \\frac{1}{y - 8} =y\\]\" width=\"277\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>If we group and combine the terms of the form  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51982d1ec35c147d9a333924065b516293dc99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"11\" /> and   <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/490ae20719cb2bc64b4d6da7fad5e72729117b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, we get this equation:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5d95ecf697346f8470038b64c0b39840b4f846a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2y}{y^2 - 64} + \\frac{2y}{y^2 - 36} = y\\]\" width=\"176\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Then, we can cancel out a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> from both sides, knowing that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/1/f71d74d90f04d0fa1dd2e326d6cf9575e308e790.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" /> is not a possible solution given the answer format.\nAfter we do that, we can make the final substitution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40b0edfcf644340a68c803e94cd260a0c9c3045e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a1eaaabe772b223c89d686645713b011e89f38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2}{z - 64} + \\frac{2}{z - 36} = 1\\]\" width=\"160\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d34a8535e161c38eee15587630703369c939c2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2z - 128 + 2z - 72 = (z - 64)(z - 36)\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce50b4cd9c9e8f4a710d00d80f6e0bca4a22ba14.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4z -  200 = z^2 - 100z + 64(36)\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509ab8d1c7b71e6b8223548c866ea11354049924.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z^2 - 104z + 2504 = 0\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Using the quadratic formula, we get that the largest solution for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/8116e7c2ca8d8dfb4b2484a93218b2c4967378b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 52 + 10\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"18\" />. Then, repeatedly substituting backwards, we find that the largest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/c/32cd67f8dda049a42b2a66320fadeb63a6e546c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + \\sqrt{52 + \\sqrt{200}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"141\" height=\"32\" />. The answer is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/323830e5c6fccff269d56ad6f6fd3c754528ec7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 + 52 + 200 = \\boxed{263}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p><br />\nNote: When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is barely larger than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/03086c52d607f04b0e679d660144b64d8662f4b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19}{x-19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" /> is very large, so the left side of the equation approaches infinity as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> from the side greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, we also know as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> gets very large, the fractions get smaller as the left side approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since the quadratic on the right side is increasing and positive when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/3/5838ed5b3cc72d400e4e782e6def348bb1b362af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, the equation will be true at a certain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4786743ea3fea48fc5858486246d374b317026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;19.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> So, we don't have to assume there is an answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/b/acbc84e38fcf36b728033e68ab60cb4be6fee9d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed as with Solution 1 until we get the following.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92ac468268cf1a985764cec42c11f7b9bcd61f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2y}{y^2 - 64} + \\frac{2y}{y^2 - 36} = y \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"225\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7b37e2578451a82b2ca0a5c0b6b3a3c2169b08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{y^2 - 64} + \\frac{1}{y^2 - 36} = \\frac{1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"189\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Here, we may also use a slightly different substitution, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/b/b8bb75ee9e4a756702f6a845746c7b4215d7eb30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = y^2 - 50.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> This gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/d/19d4a1695a4532ed127ad6f17a3bc9653f50e8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{z - 14} + \\frac{1}{z + 14} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"213\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f40dad9c793dbc32100b44ebd8d38f79718dce0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2z}{z^2 - 196} = \\frac{1}{2} \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"154\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/b/e6b48e3adbdbaa2a4494a2587aa1043da65106c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^2 - 4z - 196 = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We now have a simpler quadratic, eliminating tedious and potentially error-prone calculations. Following through, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/6/1a69b015b557f9e5bd0556ffc010d7c63d2c84a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 2 + \\sqrt{200} \\implies y = \\sqrt{52 + \\sqrt{200}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"293\" height=\"35\" /> as desired.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Stolen from forums\n</p><p>\\begin{align}\n&amp; \\frac{3}{x-3}+\\frac{5}{x-5}+\\frac{17}{x-17}+\\frac{19}{x-19}={{x}^{2}}-11x-4 \\\\\n&amp; x-11=u\\Rightarrow x=u+11 \\\\\n&amp; \\Rightarrow \\frac{3}{u+8}+\\frac{5}{u+6}+\\frac{17}{u-6}+\\frac{19}{u-8}=(u+11)u-4 \\\\\n&amp; \\Rightarrow \\frac{3(u-8)+19(u+8)}{{{u}^{2}}-64}+\\frac{5(u-6)+17(u+6)}{{{u}^{2}}-36}={{u}^{2}}+11u-4 \\\\\n&amp; \\Rightarrow \\frac{22u+128}{{{u}^{2}}-64}+\\frac{22u+72}{{{u}^{2}}-36}={{u}^{2}}+11u-4 \\\\\n&amp; \\Rightarrow \\frac{2({{u}^{2}}+11u)}{{{u}^{2}}-64}+\\frac{2({{u}^{2}}+11u)}{{{u}^{2}}-36}={{u}^{2}}+11u \\\\\n&amp; \\Rightarrow \\left\\{ \\begin{matrix}\n{{u}^{2}}+11u=0\\Rightarrow u=0,-11 \\\\\n\\frac{2}{{{u}^{2}}-64}+\\frac{2}{{{u}^{2}}-36}=1\\Rightarrow ({{u}^{2}}-36)({{u}^{2}}-64)=4{{u}^{2}}-200 \\\\\n\\end{matrix} \\right. \\\\\n&amp; {{u}^{4}}-104{{u}^{2}}+2504=0\\Rightarrow {{u}^{2}}=52\\pm 10\\sqrt{2} \\\\\n&amp; \\Rightarrow u=\\pm \\sqrt{52\\pm 10\\sqrt{2}}\\Rightarrow x=11\\pm \\sqrt{52\\pm 10\\sqrt{2}}\n\\end{align}\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first consider adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to each fraction, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae193e7c50009fca5f1d11fd944a674a0350a2c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x}{x-3} + \\frac{x}{x-5} + \\frac{x}{x-17} + \\frac{x}{x-19} = x^2-11x\\]\" width=\"358\" height=\"32\" />. We now divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> on both sides to yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/b/77ba3e0467080bed5ef533fbe83029eeb5609429.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{x-3}+\\frac{1}{x-5}+\\frac{1}{x-17}+\\frac{1}{x-19} = x-11\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"37\" />. Next, consider grouping the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c88ace77a56257b18aeef9914a0c8d9824bf45cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e411569a0df29466754693f4db515d5e8c0b74b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x-19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" />, as well as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc6b04412782976867e3f0270fee5859ef79362a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x-5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/30125509b2cb07cf0440c8c4777f9ec5c2b64bf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x-17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"57\" height=\"40\" />. If we combine these, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/72272cb88a75cdac63e0353e7daa15177e20b329.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{2x-22}{(x-3)(x-19)} + \\frac{2x-22}{(x-15)(x-7)} = x-11\\]\" width=\"343\" height=\"41\" />. Now, let us divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf4f08ce22ea06eab8b784690168c48474f2b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x-22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> on both sides to yield <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14cfe24d46adb13cfc703fbbc4e441fab104831.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{(x-3)(x-19)} + \\frac{1}{(x-15)(x-7)} = \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"305\" height=\"41\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/3/223a26777edd73a78d01f5e71365ce70027a012f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(x-3)(x-19)+(x-15)(x-17)}{(x-3)(x-19)(x-5)(x-17)} = \\frac{1}{2}\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"43\" />. Doing a bit of algebra bash yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/028a85449076df1fb8e6cdf01cc1bb12246f1b13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(2x^2-44x+142)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" /> on the LHS after also cross multiplying. As for the RHS, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/4/8f4f03dbe1c3001b82de71d57b8577d197da443d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x^2-22x+85)(x^2-22x+57)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"248\" height=\"21\" />. Now, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/7/057d1825681b38a7f9303115a658415f15dd1b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x^2-22x+71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/0/0207352dbb44d90303c5f69870f05d9e3d67f999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(2a)=(a-14)(a+14)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"196\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f41b744792de156400f5d0c3fa9c2a9e4308235.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2-4a-196$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fe79b8e3f1c301cfd8948e4bca4f288b5741a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2+10\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb098789b4d4a74c2c92825ad88c225dc7bb190.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2-10\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"109\" height=\"21\" />. We drop the latter as it is smaller. Next, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc29fe0241d6270f6f157154d3767652053b935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+10\\sqrt{2}=x^2-22x+71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"209\" height=\"21\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c32c90cb81ffbf2609e5bdcea5b84dc4dc6c59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-22x+(69-10\\sqrt2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"24\" />. We now complete the square to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b3f428107c6ed01998aef1f4444991a563bb0c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-11)^2 - 52 -10\\sqrt2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"213\" height=\"24\" />. Bringing that to the RHS gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd105b135d8f669803638477faf8947516e821ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-11)^2=52+10\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"181\" height=\"24\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/4/804fa87e94962dd4dee437f38301b9f0df749a76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=11+\\sqrt{52+10\\sqrt{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"177\" height=\"35\" />. However, we need to expand the last square root to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/9/a697aa72e3c52acdaacd6a248ebcd512ad04de85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=11+\\sqrt{52+\\sqrt{200}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"177\" height=\"35\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cb77ce35718f6021d1148f45559bb479816cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c=11+52+200=263$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"255\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>~chargren17242\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/pNsmv333SE0\">https://youtu.be/pNsmv333SE0</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity_.28Pure_magic.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathematical_Dexterity_(Pure_magic!)\">Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity (Pure magic!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathematical Dexterity (Pure magic!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7b7IPOYZbrk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7b7IPOYZbrk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution:_Math_Bear_presents..._A_Fun_Algebra_Equation_Problem\">Video Solution: Math Bear presents... A Fun Algebra Equation Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution: Math Bear presents... A Fun Algebra Equation Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hdYnbm4Tvo\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1hdYnbm4Tvo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I\" title=\"2014 AIME I\">2014 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2014\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2014 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow